2026. Price is 16$ in Kazakhstan, of course worth to buy! It's Metal Gear! :D
BUT!!! Huge BUT. This game has problems in many aspects, I am not enjoying as I would in age of 10-13 ...
Everything is fine in game, but a few things that you might feel:
1. mouse Keyboard is awful, can't make a simple things like jump or move right left in prone;
2. I am playing in Russian where many words still in English, but I saw that in English version a lot of abbreviations: PM PD WD JF BTOW PWB AWLAWIB etc... dumb as hell;
3. plot is for kids. I was about 7 years old when Metal Gear Solid came on market, was fan of MGS 1,2,3 but stopped on MGS 4, I guess because I grew up and hard to follow all of the mental problems in game;
4. YOU can finish game with starter gear. 98% of gear just "why not". 1% of gear to make game easier, 1% of fun RAMBO mode.
5. Main problem of game that it has everything and none of it in perfect quality. Grind, stealth, combat, base development, micro managment simulator, story - everything is .... OK...

I played MGS 5: The Phantom Pain for 4.5 hours and I am done, can't play it anymore.
A stealth action game must give you a motivation to play stealth: strong and smart enemies + atmosphere + exploration + empathy for the protagonist - otherwise, it's just lazy game design, "play stealth because it's a stealth game, and don't ask questions". This game gives zero motivation. Snake is a Rambo, the enemies are dummies, so you could just get your rifle and shoot them all, but even then it would still not be fun because the game is too boring:
* it's just a boring shooter, with bad, Splinter Cell like, shooting mechanics;
* the missions are boring: ride a horse in a dead desert, find, eliminate, "get to da choppa";
* same boring locations are reused for different boring missions;
* the story is for anime girls, written by the Genius himself.
One may disagree and say that "you just didn't play enough, this game will show its full potential after X hours", and I'll say that if you have to suffer for X hours to begin enjoying the game, then the game is not good.

6 years of playing this game (95% single player, not much of a FOB type.)
1 year on PS3;
3 years on PS4;
2 years of modded/retired PC (namely adding difficulty and changing things up for the unexpected.)

